    "title"             "Knox Relay"
    "description"       "Server-side bridge mod for remote server management. Exports game state, inventory snapshots, player positions, progression, live character vitals and appearance, and processes item delivery and money deposit queues via file-based JSON communication. Provides /account register for linking a character to a website account, and /report for filing a player report from inside the game."
    "changenote"        "[h1]1.23 — The Knox Desk survives being resized[/h1]\n[b]Fixed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]Dragging the window corner did not lay the desk out again. The shell replaced the resize widget's callback with one that took a width and a height, which is not the signature ISResizeWidget calls, so the drag ran a path that never fired. The override is gone; the window now relies on the size check that runs every frame, and on the minimum width and height the frame already declared.\n[*]The ticket list and the conversation panel kept the scrollbar and the line breaks they worked out when they were created. Both are now re-measured after every resize, and a panel that has been made shorter can no longer stay scrolled past its own end, which used to look like the widget had gone blank.\n[*]The reply box and the SEND button were both placed from the top of the panel, so on a short window they overlapped and the button slid off the bottom edge. Fixed-height rows are now pinned to the bottom and the thread takes whatever is left, so nothing escapes the frame at any size. The status message keeps its own column and can no longer run underneath the button.\n[*]Collapsing the window left a strip of the page hanging below the title bar. The rail and the page are now hidden while there is no room for them.\n[/list]\n[b]Changed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]The navigation rail scales with the window instead of always taking 128 pixels, so a narrow desk no longer gives a fifth of itself to the menu.\n[*]Navigation entries show an unread count as a badge and mark the open page with an accent bar, rather than appending a number to the label.\n[*]Tickets are two lines: the subject, then a coloured status pill and who the ticket is about. Unread tickets carry a marker, rows highlight under the cursor, and an empty inbox says so instead of showing an empty box.\n[/list]"
}
